  "goodToKnow": "Das Chromosom is a chromosome. Humans have 46, in 23 pairs, including the sex chromosomes X and Y. Down syndrome (Trisomie 21) results from an extra copy of chromosome 21. The name means coloured body, because chromosomes take up dye under the microscope; they were described by the German anatomist Wilhelm Waldeyer in 1888. Plural: die Chromosomen."
